.TH VHS 1 "October 2026" "vhs v0.51" "VHS for Haiku"
.SH NAME
vhs \- write terminal recordings as code on Haiku
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vhs
.I tape.tape
.br
.B vhs new
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B vhs check
.IR file | -
.br
.B vhs record
.br
.B vhs manual
.SH DESCRIPTION
VHS executes a tape script in a pseudo-terminal, maintains an in-process
VT/ANSI screen, and renders terminal sessions through Haiku's native Interface
and Translation Kits. It writes text transcripts, PNG stills and frame
sequences, and uses FFmpeg for GIF, MP4 and WebM output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new [file]
Create a starter tape without overwriting an existing file.
.TP
.B check file
Validate tape syntax without executing it. A dash reads standard input.
.TP
.B record
Record an interactive child shell as tape commands on standard output.
.TP
.B manual
Show the tape command summary.
.TP
.B version
Show the installed version.
.SH TAPE COMMANDS
.TP
.B Output path
Add a .txt, .ascii, .png, .gif, .mp4, .webm or PNG-frame-directory output.
.TP
.B Set name value
Configure shell, terminal dimensions, font, theme, timing and presentation.
The default window bar resembles Haiku Terminal. Set WindowBar Colorful for
three coloured buttons, or Set WindowBar None to hide the bar.
.TP
.B Type[@time] "text"
Type text in the child terminal. Backtick strings preserve shell backslashes.
.TP
.B Enter, Tab, Escape, Backspace, Delete, Insert, Up, Down, Left, Right
Send a key, with optional timing and repeat count.
.TP
.B Ctrl[+Alt][+Shift]+key
Send a modified key.
.TP
.B Sleep time
Advance the recording after a delay.
.TP
.B Wait[+Screen|+Line][@timeout] /expression/
Wait for terminal content to match a regular expression.
.TP
.B Hide, Show
Pause and resume transcript and frame capture.
.TP
.B Screenshot [path]
Write the current terminal frame as PNG.
.TP
.B Source path
Include another tape relative to the current tape.
.TP
.B Require program
Fail before execution when a required program is unavailable.
.TP
.B Env name value
Set an environment value in the child shell.
.TP
.B Copy "text", Paste
Write and read the Haiku system clipboard.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
The executable uses Haiku system libraries. FFmpeg must be installed for GIF,
MP4 and WebM output.
.SH FILES
Tape files conventionally use the .tape extension. See the installed VHS
documentation directory for examples and the compatibility roadmap.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. One indicates invalid input or an execution failure.
Two indicates command-line usage failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR bash (1)
